I quite agree with your sentiments, Chris, not only that it is a myth,
but that it shall remain one.  Expanding Nethack to a multi-user
setting would require changing the game from a turn-oriented timing
system to a real-time-oriented system.  This would fundamentally alter
the nature of the game.  It would have become a graphically-oriented
MUD and, however entertaining it might be, would not be Nethack.

While I'm thinking about it, what's all this shit about manipulating
bones files?  Why don't you just hack the save file?  Better yet, just
add your character to the high score list.  That way you don't have to
go through the arduous task of playing.

